  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "The current best (config_020: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc=0.725) has strong evidence supporting each component choice: imagenet_vit_l > resnet50, transformer > avgpool, and scvi_n200 > scgpt. The remaining uncertainty is whether the RNA encoder choice (scvi_n200 vs pca_n2000) still matters when paired with the strongest image encoder and aggregation. config_001 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) directly tests this: if PCA performs within ~1-2% of scvi_n200, it would offer a cheaper RNA pathway; if it drops significantly, it confirms scvi_n200 is essential and locks in the current best. This is the highest-information experiment remaining because it isolates the last untested variable in the top-performing architecture. Expected cost is moderate (~3-4 GPU hours), comparable to config_020, since PCA encoding is cheaper than scvi but the ViT-L image encoder and transformer aggregation dominate training time."
}

